never found it this whole time?

130
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,800
It seems a bit too easy.

131
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:34,240
Just hold the lantern and
keep walking. Yes, sir.

132
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,117
Now look alive, boys!

133
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,737
The treasure is near, but
so is unspeakable danger!

134
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:44,757
If you let your guard down, even for a
second, then death will creep up on you.

135
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:47,637
There's no telling what
kind of monsters will appear

136
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,777
or what vicious booby
traps await to kill us all.

137
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:54,077
Come on, men!

138
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,257
Another fine day!

139
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:56,917
Carving out tunnels awaits us.

140
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,830
Right?

141
00:07:57,913 --> 00:07:58,743
Oh, boss.

142
00:07:58,826 --> 00:08:00,400
Oh, you three must be the new guys.

143
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,657
Nothing like working up
a sweat, right, boss?

144
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:08,037
All a man really needs is a pickaxe
in his hand and a tunnel to dig.

145
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,950
That's right.

146
00:08:09,033 --> 00:08:10,897
And because of our good
old-fashioned elbow grease,

147
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,817
everyone who comes to
this tunnel will smile.

148
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:13,817
It's liberating.

149
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,317
You know, after all this, hardly.

150
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:18,694
But we ought to hit it with
the old bilge barge for a...

151
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:21,860
How dare you make me work
like one of your lackeys!

152
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:26,997
Unfortunately, that wasn't the first dead
end we hit, and it wouldn't be the last.

153
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:30,433
We ran all over the Grand Line
looking for that treasure.

154
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,897
As if that wasn't crappy enough,

155
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:36,497
my ill-fated treasure hunts brought
me straight to a navy post one day,

156
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:40,168
and the bastards threw me in
this dump when they captured me.

157
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:45,920
But maybe it was destiny all along,
guiding me to Captain John's treasure.

158
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:47,357
Step on it, stride.

159
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,734
Hard times are wasted.

160
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:52,185
Follow me and we'll be
at level two in no time.

161
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:53,380
Level two?

162
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:54,577
Were you listening to me?

163
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:56,778
I said I wanted to go to level five.

164
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:58,777
Don't you know how numbers work?

165
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:02,160
You gotta go through two to
get to five. Let me explain.

166
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,537
Think of this as an upside-down tower.

167
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:08,717
The place we're in right now is called level
one, which is the first basement floor.

168
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:11,577
After that, you go to level
two and level three and so on.

169
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:14,954
The deeper you get, the more
infamous the criminals are.

170
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:18,517
They tortured me in the fires
of level four a few times,

171
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,657
but that's as far as I've gone myself.

172
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:23,597
Everything else is just things
I've heard from other people.

173
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:26,217
Level five is where they take
all the big shots, though.

174
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,947
So in a bounty as high as your
brother's, he's gotta be there.

175
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,780
As for what's below level 5,

176
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:38,677
well, I've heard some rumors,
but the details are scarce.

177
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:41,237
The theory is the criminals
they send down there are so

178
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,277
dangerous that they've been
completely wiped from history.

179
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,597
Now that I think about it,

180
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:48,377
there's a good chance that's
where they took your brother.

181
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:52,437
But the furthest I can take you is level
4, so you're on your own after that.

182
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,460
Thanks, Buggy.

183
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:56,914
I thought you were a real
jerk, but I guess I was wrong.

184
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,300
A deal's a deal.

185
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,897
And if that armor leads me
to Captain John's treasure,

186
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,862
I'm getting a real bargain, kid.

187
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:06,060
I shouldn't have opened my big mouth.

188
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,517
If you got caught, you're
a pretty crappy pirate.

189
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,430
What the hell, man?

190
00:10:09,513 --> 00:10:10,441
Give me a break.

191
